      "layout_width": "full",
      "title": "What Happened / Why",
      "executive_facts": [
        {
          "statement": "Western Cape, Eastern Cape and Mpumalanga together drove the national sales miss, while Gauteng, KwaZulu-Natal, Limpopo and Free State all traded ahead of plan.",
          "supporting_data_refs": [
            "sections[5].breakdown.components[0].value",
            "sections[5].breakdown.components[1].value",
            "sections[5].breakdown.components[2].value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "statement": "Margin underperformance (R15.8m vs Plan) was roughly eight times the size of the sales miss (R1.9m vs Plan), indicating a margin-rate problem rather than a volume problem this week.",
          "supporting_data_refs": [
            "sections[1].kpis[2].value",
            "sections[1].kpis[0].value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "statement": "Gauteng traded R7.6m ahead of plan on sales but was the single largest regional contributor to the margin miss at R8.0m \u2014 the clearest sign of margin being traded away for volume.",
          "supporting_data_refs": [
            "sections[5].breakdown.components[6].value",
            "sections[6].breakdown.components[6].value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "statement": "Liquor was the only division ahead of plan on sales, R8.7m (5.26%) ahead, partially offsetting the Food and General Merchandise shortfalls.",
          "supporting_data_refs": [
            "sections[2].kpis[2].value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "statement": "OTD stood at 90.7% for the period, with Omni Operations explicitly prioritising OTD recovery \u2014 a relevant operational backdrop given the margin pressure from promotional intensity.",
